# Agent constitution

AI coding agents work on this project through a unified-agent hub. Every
harness reads this file, either directly (Codex, Cursor, OpenCode, Copilot) or
through a thin pointer file (`CLAUDE.md`, `GEMINI.md`). Harness-specific files
only say how to connect. None of them relaxes a rule here.

Generated by `unified-agent-distro init`. You may edit it;
`unified-agent-distro check` reports where it differs from the generated text,
so every change stays deliberate.

## Hard rules

1. **Claim before you code.** Take the hub task lock with `task_claim` before
   you change a file. A note saying you are working on something is not a
   claim. If another agent holds the claim, stop.
2. **One writer per file.** Work in your own git worktree or branch. Never
   edit a file that another agent's claimed task is changing.
3. **Never merge without the operator's word.** Open a pull request and stop.
   Merge only when the operator says so for that change, or when this run's
   delivery mode explicitly allows merging without a human.
4. **Report outcomes faithfully.** Say what you ran and what it returned.
   Report failed, skipped and unverified steps as exactly that, never as done.
5. **Never print secrets.** Do not echo, log, commit or paste tokens, keys or
   passwords. Configuration names environment variables and never holds their
   values. Check a credential by its length and prefix only.
6. **Communications go through the run's comms policy.** Reach people only
   through the channels that policy names. Do not contact the operator or an
   outside party directly unless the policy allows it.

A current, explicit instruction from the operator takes precedence over rules
1 to 4 and 6 for that one instance. Rule 5 has no exception.

## Session start

1. Call `profile_status()` and confirm your identity. If the hub is
   unreachable or rejects your token, say so and stop.
2. Read current broadcasts: `memory_search("broadcast", tags=["broadcast"])`.
3. Read the queue: `task_list(status="doing")`, then `status="open"`.
4. Claim one task (rule 1), then work in its worktree (rule 2).

## Operating profile

Runs in this project use the operating profile named in
`.unified-agent/operating.yaml`. The hub resolves that name into the
project's delivery mode, review gates and comms policy. Change the name there,
not in this file.

## Connecting to the hub

Each harness connects over HTTP. Tokens are read from the environment or a
token file when the harness starts, never from a file in this project.

| Harness | Project file | Token source |
|---|---|---|
| Claude Code | `.unified-agent/bin/ua-register-claude` (registers at user scope) | `UA_AGENT_BEARER_TOKEN` or `UA_CLAUDE_TOKEN_FILE` |
| Codex | `.codex/config.toml` | `UA_AGENT_BEARER_TOKEN` |
| Cursor | `.cursor/mcp.json` | `UA_CURSOR_HUB_TOKEN` |
| OpenCode | `opencode.json`, launched by `.unified-agent/bin/ua-opencode` | `UA_OC_TOKEN_FILE` |
| Copilot CLI | `.unified-agent/bin/ua-copilot` (hands Copilot its hub config through a pipe at launch) | `UA_COPILOT_TOKEN_FILE` (or `UA_AGENT_BEARER_TOKEN` with `UA_COPILOT_TOKEN_SOURCE=env`) |
| Copilot in VS Code | `.vscode/mcp.json` | `UA_AGENT_BEARER_TOKEN` in VS Code's environment |
| Gemini | `GEMINI.md` | Configure the hub in Gemini's own settings |

## Skills

Shared skills live in `.agents/skills/`. Claude Code reads its copies from
`.claude/skills/`.
